proof.text:
(Free modules have depth $\ge d$.) Let $n\ge1$ and $F=R^{\oplus n}$, a nonzero finite free $R$-module [def-weil-pbc-free-module]. As $R$ is local, $\mathfrak mR=\mathfrak m
eq R$, so by [def-weil-pbc-depth] $\operatorname{depth}(R)$ is the supremum of the lengths of $R$-regular sequences in $\mathfrak m$, and $\operatorname{depth}(R)\ge d$ gives an $R$-regular sequence $g_1,\dots,g_r$ in $\mathfrak m$ with $r\ge d$ [def-weil-pbc-regular-sequence]. Put $f_i=g_i$ for $i\le d$ and $I_i=(f_1,\dots,f_i)$. For every ideal $I$ one has $F/IF=(R/I)^{\oplus n}$ componentwise, and multiplication by $f_i$ on $F/I_{i-1}F=(R/I_{i-1})^{\oplus n}$ is multiplication by $f_i$ on each component, injective because $f_i$ is a nonzerodivisor on $R/I_{i-1}$ ($i\le d\le r$); and $F/I_dF=(R/I_d)^{\oplus n}
eq0$ because $I_d\subset\mathfrak m$ and $n\ge1$. So $f_1,\dots,f_d$ is an $F$-regular sequence in $\mathfrak m$, and $\mathfrak mF
eq F$ ($F/\mathfrak mF=(R/\mathfrak m)^{\oplus n}
eq0$); hence $\operatorname{depth}(F)\ge d$. Depth is invariant under isomorphism of modules (an isomorphism $F\cong F'$ induces isomorphisms $F/IF\cong F'/IF'$ compatible with multiplication by elements of $R$), so every finite free module $\cong R^{\oplus n}$, $n\ge1$, has depth $\ge d$.
